.TH MU2EDAQ-FILE-REAPER-STOP 1 "2026-09-11" "mu2edaq-file-reaper 0.1.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
stop-mu2edaq-file-reaper.sh \- stop the file reaper daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B stop-mu2edaq-file-reaper.sh
[\fIPIDFILE\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Standardised Mu2e control-room stop script, run by
.BR "crs-app stop file-reaper" .
It sends SIGTERM to every copy of the reaper running out of the script's
directory (found through the PID file and the process table, see
.BR mu2edaq-file-reaper-start (1)),
waits up to
.B CRS_STOP_TIMEOUT
seconds for the daemon to finish the file it is working on, then sends
SIGKILL, and removes the PID file.  A stale PID file naming an unrelated live
process is cleaned up without signalling that process.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I PIDFILE
PID file to consult (default
.IR ./file-reaper.pid ).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CRS_STOP_TIMEOUT
Grace period in seconds before SIGKILL (default 30).
.SH EXIT STATUS
Always 0 unless the shell itself fails.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2edaq-file-reaper-start (1),
.BR mu2edaq-file-reaper (1)
